107	使用於地圖分析、交通規劃與旅遊建議，雙北的自行車路網可與其他圖資套疊，提供更深入的洞察。透過將自行車道與人口密度、交通流量或公車捷運路線交叉比對，可優化城市規劃，提高自行車友善程度。對於旅遊應用，可將自行車道與景點、商圈、飯店位置結合，推薦最佳騎行路線，提升遊憩體驗。此外，政府與企業可藉由數據分析發掘需求熱點，進一步優化自行車基礎設施與共享單車系統。	en	Used in map analysis, transportation planning, and travel recommendations, the bike lane network in the Taipei metropolitan area can be overlaid with other map data to provide deeper insights. By cross-referencing bike lanes with population density, traffic volume, or bus and metro routes, urban planning can be optimized and bike-friendliness can be improved. For tourism applications, bike lanes can be combined with attractions, commercial districts, and hotel locations to recommend the best cycling routes and enhance the recreational experience. Additionally, the government and businesses can use data analysis to identify areas of high demand and further optimize bike infrastructure and bike-sharing systems.	use_case	2026-05-02 10:47:07.514065+00
108	顯示雙北當前自行車路網分布。雙北擁有完善的自行車路網，主要包括河濱自行車道和市區自行車道。河濱自行車道沿淡水河、基隆河、新店溪和景美溪等河岸建設，提供連續且風景優美的騎行路線。市區自行車道則遍布於主要道路，如敦化南北路、成功路、承德路、松隆路、松德路、和平西路、民生東路、北安路、金湖路、八德路、大道路、光復南路和永吉路等，方便市民在城市中安全騎行。此外，雙北政府持續推動「自行車道願景計畫」，以串聯既有路網、銜接跨市及河濱自行車道，並優化現有自行車道，提升騎行環境的便利性與安全性。	en	It shows the current distribution of bicycle lanes in the Taipei metropolitan area. The Taipei metropolitan area has a complete network of bicycle lanes, mainly including riverside bicycle paths and urban bicycle paths. The riverside bicycle paths are built along the banks of the Tamsui River, Keelung River, Xindian River, and Jingmei River, providing continuous and scenic riding routes. The urban bicycle paths are distributed on major roads, such as Dunhua North and South Roads, Chenggong Road, Chengde Road, Songlong Road, Songde Road, Heping West Road, Minsheng East Road, Beian Road, Jinhua Road, Bade Road, Dadao Road, Guangfu South Road, and Yongji Road, making it convenient for citizens to ride safely in the city. In addition, the Taipei metropolitan area government continues to promote the "Bicycle Path Vision Plan" to connect existing networks, link up with cross-city and riverside bicycle paths, and optimize existing bicycle paths to improve the convenience and safety of the riding environment.	long_desc	2026-05-02 10:47:10.392223+00
